From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: start and go on only once the display has
 changed mode

A display mode change drops the sound of the HDMI link, and the TV, and a
receiver behind it (over eARC, twice over), take a while to find it again;
whatever plays meanwhile is lost. Playback started before the refresh rate
change it had queued, so every film whose mode changed lost its first
sound, and the display coming back unpaused the player at once.

Playback now starts only once a refresh rate change Kodi has queued is
made, or one the platform says is coming (ProcessInfo), five seconds at
most. After each mode change the player stays paused for the new setting
"Wait after a display change" (1.5 s by default), the audio output sending
silence the chain locks on to, then sound and picture start together.

Shared code, unavoidable: only CVideoPlayer starts playback and handles
the display coming back; the render manager is the one that knows a
refresh rate change is queued.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
index 48151fd..26550d3 100644
--- a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
+++ b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
@@ -9191,6 +9191,18 @@ msgctxt "#60025"
 msgid "Passthrough Audio"
 msgstr ""
 
+#. Setting: how long playback waits after the display changes mode
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#60120"
+msgid "Wait after a display change"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Help text for setting #60120 "Wait after a display change"
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#60121"
+msgid "When the display changes mode, the TV and any receiver behind it take a moment to find the sound again, and whatever plays meanwhile is lost. Playback stays paused this long after each change, sound and picture then starting together. Lower it until the first words get clipped, then go one step back up."
+msgstr ""
+
 #: xbmc/music/MusicDatabase.cpp
 #: xbmc/video/VideoDatabase.cpp
 msgctxt "#15011"
